# Architecture & Laravel Standards

This is a Laravel 13 / PHP 8.5 / Livewire 3 app. Prefer current Laravel conventions (Form Requests, Actions/Services, thin controllers, Eloquent).

## SOLID / SRP

- One clear responsibility per class/method; extract Services, Actions, or Traits when logic grows.
- Controllers orchestrate; they do not own business rules, queries, or formatting.
- Prefer small, composable methods over large multi-purpose blocks.

## Avoid redundancy (DRY)

- Before adding helpers, queries, or UI patterns, search the codebase for existing Services, Traits, scopes, Livewire components, and Blade partials.
- Reuse and extend what exists; do not duplicate near-identical logic.

## Imports & namespaces

- Always `use` classes at the top of the file.
- Never call classes via fully qualified inline names like `\App\Models\User::...` when an import works.

```php
// ❌ BAD
$user = \App\Models\User::find($id);

// ✅ GOOD
use App\Models\User;
$user = User::find($id);
```

## Eloquent over query builder / DB facade

- Prefer Eloquent models, relationships, and scopes.
- Use `DB::` / raw SQL only when Eloquent is clearly unsuitable; justify briefly if doing so.
- Prefer eager loading (`with`) to avoid N+1 queries.

## Formatting

- Use at most one blank line between logical blocks; never stacks of empty lines.
- Match surrounding file style; keep diffs focused.

## Clarify before guessing

- If requirements, edge cases, or the right reuse target are unclear, ask before implementing.
